# Milestone: v0.13.3
# Covers: bare float argument to every() means SECONDS (refactor-3 SCHED-14).
#
# Pre-fix: the float period was coerced to microseconds via (uint64_t)f, so
#   every(0.05) produced period_us = 0, causing the body to fire on every
#   scheduler pump pass instead of every 50ms.
# Post-fix: float period is treated as SECONDS (matching sleep()), so
#   every(0.05) = every(50ms) = period_us = 50000.
#
# Script installs every(0.05) { ... }, then drives the virtual clock forward
# in two 50ms increments.  The body must fire exactly once per increment
# (fixed cadence, no burst), so Realm.fired reaches 2 after two periods.
#
## timeout: 30
## host: run Realm.fired = 0
## host: run every (0.05) { Realm.fired = Realm.fired + 1 }
## host: run Realm.fired
## host: advance-clock 50
## host: step 100000
## host: run Realm.fired
## host: advance-clock 50
## host: step 100000
## host: run Realm.fired
[00000000] 0
[00000000] nil
[00000000] 0
[00000000] step: WAKE_AT
[00000000] 1
[00000000] step: WAKE_AT
[00000000] 2
